@startuml
title SEQ-11 - Controlled Migration and Deployment
autonumber
actor Owner as "Release Owner"
participant CI
participant Backup
control Migrator
database DB
control Core
control GotIt
control Web
control Chrome as "Chrome Store Candidate"
participant Monitor

Owner -> CI: Approve exact commits and release scope
CI -> CI: Typecheck/lint/unit/contract/build/security checks
break Quality gate fails
  CI --> Owner: Block release with evidence
end
Owner -> Backup: Create managed + schema backup
Backup --> Owner: Backup identifier verified
Owner -> Migrator: Run preflight/normalization audit
Migrator -> DB: Read-only compatibility checks
Migrator --> Owner: Expected baseline
Owner -> Migrator: Run additive migration with dedicated credential
Migrator -> DB: Advisory lock + forward migrations
Migrator --> Owner: Version and verification result
alt Migration fails
  Owner -> Owner: Stop deployment, assess restore/forward-fix
else Migration succeeds
  Owner -> Core: Deploy compatible Core if required
  Owner -> GotIt: Deploy product backend
  GotIt -> DB: Startup schema/privilege check
  Owner -> Web: Deploy gateway/client
  Owner -> Chrome: Build/package candidate (store release may lag)
  par Health and readiness
    Monitor -> Core: /health and /ready
    Monitor -> GotIt: /health and /ready
    Monitor -> Web: /health and /ready
  end
  Owner -> Monitor: Authenticated smoke critical flows
  alt Smoke/metrics fail
    Owner -> Owner: Roll back compatible images or forward-fix\nDo not run destructive down migration blindly
  else Healthy
    Owner -> Owner: Record evidence, version and status
  end
end
note over Owner,DB
Runtime and migrator credentials must be separated.
Production completion requires live acceptance, not only CI success.
end note
@enduml

